NEARS-3441 QA — AC-add (module-mismatch -> 404) Data DoR gap

Query (READ-ONLY, SELECT/JOIN only) across every coupon-bearing order in the
seeded multi_food_db:

  SELECT o.id, o.coupon_code, o.store_id, s.module_id AS store_module,
         c.module_id AS coupon_module
  FROM orders o
  JOIN stores s ON s.id=o.store_id
  LEFT JOIN coupons c ON c.code = o.coupon_code
  WHERE o.coupon_code IS NOT NULL AND o.coupon_code != ''
    AND (c.module_id IS NULL OR c.module_id != s.module_id);

  -> 0 rows. All 14 coupon-bearing orders in seed data carry a coupon whose
     module_id already matches their own store's module_id (all module 1 =
     Grocery & Food). No naturally-occurring module-mismatch order exists to
     drive live through the real Store Panel web UI without a DB write (out
     of scope for read-only QA -- and even placing a NEW order through the
     app's own customer flow would not reproduce it, since normal checkout
     already validates the coupon's module against the cart's module before
     the order is ever created; this scenario is a defense-in-depth branch
     for historical drift, e.g. a store's module_id reassigned after the
     order/coupon existed -- not a state reachable through a live legitimate
     order-placement flow either).

Verdict: UNVERIFIABLE (live web UI) -- Data DoR gap, not a code defect.

Supporting evidence (not a substitute for the live demo, but materially
de-risks it):
1. Code-level: CouponLogic::is_valide() lines 45-48 (the 404 module-mismatch
   branch) is NOT new/untested logic -- it is unconditionally exercised in
   normal production traffic by the customer-facing coupon-apply API
   (Api/V1/CouponController.php:100) and by the vendor-API order-amount-edit
   twin (Api/V1/Vendor/VendorController.php:1078, via the
   config('module.current_module_data') fallback populated by
   VendorTokenIsValid middleware on that surface). The NEARS-3441 fix simply
   threads the same $store variable this function already uses elsewhere in
   the same call (store_wise / created_by=vendor branches, lines 66-73) into
   the module_id argument -- not new code shape.
2. Automated backstop: tests/Feature/Security/Nears3441VendorCouponModuleIdTest.php
   ::test_coupon_module_mismatch_returns_404() constructs a fixture coupon
   with module_id = store's module_id + 1 and asserts the controller
   response is exactly 404 with no exception thrown. Ran live this session:
   4/4 tests, 10 assertions, PASS (see automated backstop in envelope).

Followup filed: seed a real coupon+order pair with a genuine module_id
mismatch (e.g. a Pharmacy-module coupon attached to a Grocery-module store's
order) so this AC-add can be demonstrated live end-to-end in a future pass.
